rsx_live_draw: full guest sampler state (border colour, anisotropy, LOD bias, convolution as linear) and a
lossless sampler cache key.

decode_sampler read only min/mag/mip filter and the LOD range: TEXTURE_BORDER_COLOR was ignored (BORDER wrap
sampled black), as were anisotropy (CONTROL0 [6:4]), LOD bias (FILTER [12:0], signed 4.8) and the convolution
filters (min 7 / mag 4 fell to point). sampler_key packed a 21-bit LOD field at bit 18 of one u32, dropping its
top bits, so different LOD ranges shared one descriptor, and it omitted bias/aniso/border. Now the same mapping
as rsx_d3d12_backend.c's patch-2001 sampler, keyed on four words (filter, wrap, control0, border when used).
Test: tools/smoke/host_kz3.c --live (four sampler quads through the live engine) under GE-Proton: the BORDER
quad (unit 15, white border colour) was black, now white; the other three unchanged. KZ3 port RSX, 2026-10-07.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): partly absorbed, PR321 keys filter, wrap and LOD, ours adds bias, aniso and border colour which our sampler decode reads, ours kept.

